  "tagline": "In-memory RDF store with incremental Datalog reasoning, now owned by Samsung.",
  "description": "RDFox is a high-performance, in-memory RDF triple store and Datalog reasoner developed at the University of Oxford and commercialized by Oxford Semantic Technologies, which Samsung Electronics acquired in 2024. Its distinguishing feature is incremental materialization: rules and OWL 2 RL axioms are re-evaluated efficiently as data changes, so queries see up-to-date inferences without full recomputation. It runs as a server or embedded library, including an Android build used on Samsung Galaxy devices. Choose it when rule-based reasoning speed matters more than raw dataset size.",
